addressing russian ambassadors gathered  in moscow vladimir putin distanced  himself from events unfolding in eastern  ukraine he also implied the new  administration in kiev is making a grave  mistake  unfortunately president poroshenko  decided to resume his military operation  when i say we i mean both myself and my  european colleagues  we were not able to convince him that  the road to sustainable solid and  lasting peace cannot lead through war  publicly at least moscow had been  pushing for an extension to the  ukrainian government ceasefire before it  expired putin also offered poroshenko to  let ukraine monitor border checkpoints  but poroshenko said the separatists had  only used the ceasefire to regroup  we will liberate our land  the decision not to extend the ceasefire  is our response to terrorists rebels and  marauders to all those who terrorize  civilians  the government's 10-day long ceasefire  in eastern ukraine was never really  effective fighting continued and both  sides blamed each other for the violence  on the weekend the ukrainian security  service arrested men it suspects of  trying to bomb a railway track near  kharkiv  this and attacks on government forces  has made ukrainians question separatists  commitment to peace talks  germany's foreign minister has expressed  disappointment at the end of the  ukrainian ceasefire  but he told a dw media event he hopes  that more talks will produce results in  the coming days  i think it would be good to build on the  limited dialogue that's taken place so  far between russian and ukrainian  authorities  if we were to continue and to intensify  those efforts then perhaps joint border  controls would result  that would prevent weapons and fighters  crossing over ukraine's eastern border  but for now diplomacy has been sidelined  amid more violence in eastern ukraine
 

